WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.550
The awesome second season of The Umbrella
Academy just exploded onto our screens with

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:09.990
the gang arriving in the 60s to meddle with
the timeline, stop a new apocalypse, and leave

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:13.010
us with yet another epic cliffhanger for Season
3.

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:17.289
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video we're breaking down everything

00:00:17.289 --> 00:00:21.739
you need to know about that big twist ending,
including clues you might have missed about

00:00:21.739 --> 00:00:26.819
the new characters, upgraded Umbrella Academy
powers, and what it all means for Season 3!

00:00:26.819 --> 00:00:30.750
It goes without saying spoilers ahead, so
take care.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:34.550
Season 2 ends on an all-mighty cliffhanger
when the Umbrella Academy return from the

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:39.230
60s to 2019 only to discover things are not
as they expected.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:43.210
Not only is there a portrait of Ben on the
wall at the academy where the portrait of

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:48.449
Five used to be, but their father Reginald
Hargreeves is still alive and he drops this

00:00:48.449 --> 00:00:50.629
bombshell:
"This isn't your home.

00:00:50.629 --> 00:00:52.500
This is the Sparrow Academy."

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:57.589
A mystery group of five assemble above and
Ben 2.0 strides into view:

00:00:57.589 --> 00:01:00.269
"Dad, who the hell are these assholes?"

00:01:00.269 --> 00:01:04.809
This is a huge WTF moment for the Umbrella
Academy who suddenly discover they have no

00:01:04.809 --> 00:01:06.790
home and no obvious future.

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:11.090
First off, some interesting details to point
out are that Ben, who is of course alive in

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:14.220
this new timeline,
seems to be the Sparrow Academy leader, the

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:17.710
equivalent of the Umbrella crew's Luther aka
Number One.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:22.410
Notice the scar on his face, which he presumably
acquired on a mission, and also the coat of

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:27.490
arms on his jacket which has a sparrow in
the top-left quarter rather than an umbrella.

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:31.250
Something else you might have missed is a
mystery cube that floats into view next to

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:33.060
the other Sparrows on the balcony.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:37.590
The cube has some glowing green light inside
and although it could be some kind of device

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:42.600
or invention the Sparrows use, it might also
be the seventh member of the team, perhaps

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:47.290
even a character who died like original Ben
and whose consciousness is contained within

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:50.480
the cube, perhaps like Robotman from Doom
Patrol.

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:55.561
Or if the cube itself is sentient, it makes
me think of the talking A.I., Mainframe, which

00:01:55.561 --> 00:01:58.740
appears in one of the Guardians of the Galaxy
2 post-credits scenes

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:00.780
"I miss you guys so much."

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:05.550
If the cube is just a piece of tech though,
I wonder if the fact there are only six Sparrows

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:10.640
on screen could imply one of them is dead
or that there's a supposedly non-powered sibling,

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:14.540
like Vanya aka Seven, who's not yet part of
their super-team.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:19.200
In the comics, the Sparrow Academy is a group
of superheroes who turn up at the very end

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.250
of the third volume of books to take down
a group of villains rampaging through the

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:24.250
city.

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:28.170
They seem more capable than the Umbrella Academy
who were basically losing the battle until

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:29.570
the Sparrows arrived.

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:32.940
Their leader calls himself "Number One" but
they have different powers to the Umbrella

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:33.940
team.

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:37.120
And the comic book Sparrows also have a cube
that floats alongside them.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:41.730
Gerard Way, the comics writer and producer
on the Netflix show, has said the next volume

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:45.810
in the comics will begin to answer questions
about the other super-babies which strongly

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:50.100
implies that the Sparrows are indeed other
babies born on that fateful day.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:54.470
The TV show will doubtless have its own plans
that will differ in some ways from the comics,

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:58.370
but what's especially interesting is that
there were sparrow motifs hidden all through

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:02.010
the second season foreshadowing the introduction
of this new team.

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:05.870
And you can see those secret sparrows in my
upcoming "Things You Missed" video.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:08.709
But how did the Sparrow Academy come about?

00:03:08.709 --> 00:03:14.270
Was Reginald Hargreeves so unimpressed with
the Umbrella team he met in 1963 that he decided

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:17.160
to form an alternative super-group: the Sparrow
Academy?

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:18.569
"Thank you for coming.

00:03:18.569 --> 00:03:20.130
I've seen about enough."

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:24.630
Or did the Umbrella crew alter the timeline
so badly in Season 2 that they accidentally

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:26.480
wrote themselves out of the future?

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:31.260
Let's review the season's big events for evidence
and how this points to the existence of an

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:33.640
Umbrella Academy multiverse.

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:37.660
One of the crucial moments in Season 2 that
connects directly to the events of the first

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:41.480
season is when Old Man Five time travels through
a portal from 1963 to 2019.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:43.490
However, when the scene plays out again in
the second season, there's a subtle but vital

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:44.490
difference.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:49.830
In Season 2, we see Old Man Five fall backwards
through the portal into 2019 rather than falling

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:52.940
through face forwards as he did in Season
1.

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:58.690
And the Five that jumps forward in time to
2019 in Season 2 also has a whole lot of different

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:01.070
information to what he had in the first season.

00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:05.440
For example, Luther already told him that
the eyeball he found in the apocalypse is

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:07.960
just a red herring:
"Yeah, that's a waste of time."

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:11.510
"Then why were you holding it when I found
you dead in the apocalypse?"

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:12.510
"No idea.

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:13.840
But the guy it belonged to didn't end the
world.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:15.050
Vanya did."

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:19.049
The eyeball Luther is referring to belonged
to Leonard and so now when Five arrives in

00:04:19.049 --> 00:04:23.930
2019 it won't make sense for him to chase
down leads on where the eye came from,

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:26.819
as he'd surely immediately tell the others
about Vanya.

00:04:26.819 --> 00:04:29.870
Which means he will end up creating an alternate
timeline.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:33.919
We've already seen the show touch on alternate
realities in the first season, for example,

00:04:33.919 --> 00:04:36.120
Episode 6 "The Day That Wasn't", where Allison
and Luther dance.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:40.780
But at the end of that episode when Five time-jumped
to an earlier point in that day, the show

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:45.139
followed on and began an alternate timeline
in which Allison and Luther never had that

00:04:45.139 --> 00:04:46.139
kiss.

00:04:46.139 --> 00:04:47.139
"We have never even kissed."

00:04:47.139 --> 00:04:52.069
And there are so many other examples in Season
2 of major effects that the super-siblings

00:04:52.069 --> 00:04:55.290
must have had on the timeline,
that it's easy to see why the gang arrive

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:57.879
back in a rather different 2019.

00:04:57.879 --> 00:05:01.779
As Vanya pointed out in the 60s:
"Has anyone done anything here to screw up

00:05:01.779 --> 00:05:02.779
the timeline?"

00:05:02.779 --> 00:05:06.789
Klaus, for example, starts a cult that attracts
at least a few hundred followers and tries

00:05:06.789 --> 00:05:09.639
to convince Dave not to sign up to fight in
Vietnam.

00:05:09.639 --> 00:05:13.810
In fact, there's a clue in the sixth episode
that the timeline was already changing when

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:18.190
Klaus discovers that Dave has enlisted in
the army days before it originally happened.

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:23.180
And by the final episode, the whole Umbrella
crew end up on the national news as persons

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:27.990
of interest in the JFK assassination, something
which could have myriad repercussions on the

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:29.090
timeline.

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:32.259
In addition to that, Five killed the Commission's
board of directors, allowing the Handler to

00:05:32.259 --> 00:05:33.259
take over.

00:05:33.259 --> 00:05:36.210
Which means the Commission's decisions on
how they want the timeline to proceed could

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:39.839
be very different now,
which could lead to the formation of The Sparrow

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:40.839
Academy.

00:05:40.839 --> 00:05:44.879
And given Reginald Hargreeves is still alive
in the new timeline, it's fair to assume that

00:05:44.879 --> 00:05:49.650
Pogo and Grace who were killed during Vanya's
destructive rampage in Season 1 will also

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:51.080
be back in Season 3.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:55.610
A crucial new character that will surely be
returning is Lila, who in the finale turned

00:05:55.610 --> 00:06:00.430
out to be one of the 43 super-powered babies
born on the same day in 1989.

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:05.639
Lila's power set is fascinating as she can
reproduce the abilities of any of the Umbrella

00:06:05.639 --> 00:06:08.050
Academy members in certain circumstances.

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:12.860
For example, when Vanya flattened the Handler's
army of assassins with an energy blast, Lila

00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:18.060
was able to replicate Vanya's defensive powers,
by creating a shield that protected both her

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:19.090
and the Handler.

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:23.569
Lila can also mirror Vanya's other powers,
such as when she sent a powerful blast against

00:06:23.569 --> 00:06:24.879
the Umbrella crew.

00:06:24.879 --> 00:06:30.100
On top of that, Lila was also able to redirect
Alison's rumour back at her, almost killing

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:31.100
her.

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:33.490
"I heard a rumor..."
"...you stopped breathing."

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:37.410
And she also took on Luther's brute strength
when he tried to hit her.

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:42.060
Although Lila's huge power reveal was a surprise
in the finale, there was actually a hint to

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:46.720
her ability to mirror other people's powers
during her mid-season fight with Five when

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:48.849
she was able to blink just like he does.

00:06:48.849 --> 00:06:50.469
"How are you doing this?"

00:06:50.469 --> 00:06:52.240
"Anything you can do, I can do better."

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:57.259
Lila's ability to mimic other hero's superpowers
reminds me of the Marvel villain Taskmaster

00:06:57.259 --> 00:06:59.360
who appears in the new Black Widow movie.

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:00.360
"So unoriginal."

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:04.050
It seems that Lila's abilities may be something
that's triggered temporarily,

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:07.930
such as when another super-powered individual
uses their powers because she doesn't seem

00:07:07.930 --> 00:07:10.330
to use superpowers any other time.

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:14.939
Lila has a troubled backstory, with Five having
killed her parents after the Handler placed

00:07:14.939 --> 00:07:18.149
a kill order on them so she could adopt the
gifted girl for herself.

00:07:18.149 --> 00:07:22.930
So, Diego suggested that she join the Umbrella
Academy who he said were her real family,

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:28.150
however, she ended up escaping with a Commission
briefcase to an unknown time and location.

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:31.520
Is it possible that Lila is one of the members
of the Sparrow Academy?

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:35.870
Either way, she's far too interesting a character
not to return at some point.

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:40.690
As for Lila's adoptive mother The Handler,
by the end of season 2 her double-dealings

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:44.770
with the Swedes and her scheming against the
Umbrella Academy finally catch up with her

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:48.169
as the sole surviving Swede guns her down.

00:07:48.169 --> 00:07:51.629
Presumably she's dead for good this time;
however, that also appeared to be the case

00:07:51.629 --> 00:07:56.129
in Season 1 when Hazel shot her in the head,
but she survived thanks to the metal plate

00:07:56.129 --> 00:07:57.129
in her head.

00:07:57.129 --> 00:08:02.099
I wouldn't quite put it past her returning
in the future as she was such a fantastic

00:08:02.099 --> 00:08:06.110
character, with her schemes and outfits getting
more and more outrageous as her powers grew

00:08:06.110 --> 00:08:09.479
within the Commission;
though I suspect if she does reappear, it'll

00:08:09.479 --> 00:08:12.699
be in flashbacks or yet another alternate
timeline.

00:08:12.699 --> 00:08:17.319
Although the Umbrella Academy's very existence
comes into question when they get back to

00:08:17.319 --> 00:08:20.600
2019,
by the end of Season 2 the team are actually

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:24.600
much stronger and more mature, with a better
understanding of who they really are and better

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:28.699
control over their powers,
which will be important for Season 3.

00:08:28.699 --> 00:08:32.940
Vanya and Ben perhaps go through the biggest
arc with their fates converging in an emotional

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:34.399
ninth episode.

00:08:34.399 --> 00:08:39.759
When Vanya arrives in 1963, she loses her
memory after being hit by Sissy's car, so

00:08:39.759 --> 00:08:43.849
she starts with a blank slate and seems more
comfortable in her own skin than in the first

00:08:43.849 --> 00:08:44.849
season.

00:08:44.849 --> 00:08:49.240
Not surprising given that now she's not being
mistreated, constantly made to feel she's

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:52.620
worthless, or incessantly compared to her
super-siblings.

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:56.570
And as she rediscovers who she really is,
this time – unlike in Season 1

00:08:56.570 --> 00:08:59.589
she has much more control over her powers.

00:08:59.589 --> 00:09:04.380
She's able to voluntarily levitate a whole
body of water in order to rescue Harlan and

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:09.190
she breezily demonstrates how she can manipulate
a sound wave in front of Hargreeves and her

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:10.190
siblings.

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:15.089
She can even turn into the White Violin at
will as a way of warning Five, and then quickly

00:09:15.089 --> 00:09:16.190
turn it off as well.

00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:21.139
She has control over her energy blasts now
and curiously she almost seemed to make the

00:09:21.139 --> 00:09:24.870
FBI agent's face implode when he was interrogating
her.

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:29.029
However, when she's drugged by the Feds and
electro-shocked, Vanya's memories of what

00:09:29.029 --> 00:09:33.670
she did in the first season, including attacking
her sister Allison and destroying the world,

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:34.720
come flooding back.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:38.130
"You can't deny your true self even if you
are afraid".

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:42.550
And the emotional overload sends Vanya's powers
out of control again.

00:09:42.550 --> 00:09:46.819
That's when Ben becomes the hero of the moment
because, as a ghost, he's the only one who

00:09:46.819 --> 00:09:50.440
can withstand the physical force that's blasting
out from Vanya.

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:55.579
Ben uses his newfound ability of possessing
another body to enter Vanya's psyche and communicate

00:09:55.579 --> 00:09:56.579
with her.

00:09:56.579 --> 00:10:00.759
He helps his sister come to terms with her
powers, and explains that she isn't a monster

00:10:00.759 --> 00:10:04.090
and that her siblings love her and are out
there fighting to help her.

00:10:04.090 --> 00:10:08.480
The brotherly love that Ben shares with Vanya
in this moment is very touching and restores

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:12.670
her sense of self-worth, bringing her back
from the brink of destruction.

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:17.430
This experience also gives Ben the resolution
he's been looking for for 17 years to leave

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:19.170
his current plane of existence.

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:24.459
There's a really nice visual of Ben walking
towards the light as he goes to help Vanya,

00:10:24.459 --> 00:10:28.670
which relates to the conversation he had with
his brother Klaus at his own funeral:

00:10:28.670 --> 00:10:30.620
"There's a light and they told me to walk
into it."

00:10:30.620 --> 00:10:31.690
"That thing.

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:32.940
Don't worry about it."

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:34.279
"You can go whenever you want."

00:10:34.279 --> 00:10:38.769
As for the others, Klaus develops his ability
to manifest ghosts other than Ben in the real

00:10:38.769 --> 00:10:39.769
world.

00:10:39.769 --> 00:10:44.370
When Lila's blast sends him flying for a potentially
lethal fall, he summons a couple of ghosts

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.209
to catch him safely.

00:10:46.209 --> 00:10:50.850
And in the 1963 apocalypse we got a glimpse
of the potential of his powers when he summoned

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:54.620
an army of the dead.

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:58.899
Five finally masters time travel by limiting
his attempts to travel back in time to just

00:10:58.899 --> 00:11:03.110
a few seconds or minutes rather than whole
years or decades at once,

00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:08.020
and with this skill he's able to reverse everyone's
brutal deaths by the Handler.

00:11:08.020 --> 00:11:12.410
Allison was unable to speak for a year until
her throat wound healed and because she couldn't

00:11:12.410 --> 00:11:16.629
use her power, she felt more like everything
she accomplished was earned.

00:11:16.629 --> 00:11:21.089
Given the situation she lands in though, her
inability then reluctance to use her powers

00:11:21.089 --> 00:11:23.110
can feel more frustrating than usual.

00:11:23.110 --> 00:11:28.250
But as Emmy Raver-Lampman told Den of Geek,
Allison sees her power "as more of a curse

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:31.500
than a blessing" as it's "always backfired
in the long game".

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:36.040
Still, by the end of Season 2, Allison seems
to feel she's found the right balance of when

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:38.079
to call on her ability.

00:11:38.079 --> 00:11:42.720
Diego spends much of Season 2 really playing
up to his hero complex, and although it's

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:47.459
not entirely clear whether he resolved that,
his power to manipulate objects in mid-air

00:11:47.459 --> 00:11:52.140
gets an upgrade in the final showdown when
he's able to redirect an enormous hail of

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:53.290
bullets.

00:11:53.290 --> 00:11:57.940
And then there was that pretty awesome moment
during the 1963 apocalypse when if you look

00:11:57.940 --> 00:12:00.740
really closely,
Diego is bending this stream of bullets away

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:03.519
from him as he spirals through the air.

00:12:03.519 --> 00:12:08.240
In terms of their personal lives though, in
many ways the gang lose more than they gain.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:13.209
Vanya finds a soul mate in Sissy but the dangers
of life as a super-powered individual mean

00:12:13.209 --> 00:12:16.540
Sissy's scared for Harlan's safety if she
goes with Vanya.

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:19.860
However, a door is left open for a reunion
down the road:

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:22.750
"If you ever find a safe way back to me, you
take it."

00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:27.149
If Vanya wanted to leave the team or settle
down, she could grab a Commission briefcase

00:12:27.149 --> 00:12:31.400
and travel back in time to be with Sissy,
similar to how Hazel enjoyed his golden years

00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:33.060
with Agnes in another timeline.

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:36.470
Each of the others also loses someone important
to them.

00:12:36.470 --> 00:12:41.069
Diego loses Lila to the timeline, although
there's a good chance they will meet again;

00:12:41.069 --> 00:12:44.000
and Allison had to give up her marriage with
Ray.

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:47.199
Klaus wasn't able to convince Dave not to
go to Vietnam

00:12:47.199 --> 00:12:51.760
and when Ben leaves the earthly plane, he's
no longer able to see the girl he likes from

00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:52.839
Klaus's cult.

00:12:52.839 --> 00:12:57.720
As for Luther, when Jack Ruby disowns him,
he loses the father figure he never had.

00:12:57.720 --> 00:13:00.589
"I treated you like a son"

00:13:00.589 --> 00:13:05.879
Ok, time to discuss Harlan, Sissy's son, who
was gifted Vanya's telekinetic powers when

00:13:05.879 --> 00:13:08.680
she resuscitated him after he appeared to
drown.

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:12.680
Those little lights that transferred into
him seem to confirm the theory that the glowing

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:15.709
lights we saw Hargreeves release in the Season
1 finale

00:13:15.709 --> 00:13:21.750
are connected to the special powers inherited
by Vanya and likely all 43 super-babies born

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:22.980
in 1989.

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:26.990
Harlan's manifestation of powers triggers
a major alarm at the Commission, with the

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:30.579
Handler recognising the importance of the
event which is why she went immediately to

00:13:30.579 --> 00:13:33.980
take Harlan for herself, like she did with
Lila.

00:13:33.980 --> 00:13:37.939
Interestingly though, the transference of
power from Vanya to Harlan connects them both

00:13:37.939 --> 00:13:39.240
even across distances.

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:44.579
Harlan goes into a trance when Vanya is being
tortured by the FBI, and emerges from it at

00:13:44.579 --> 00:13:46.879
the same time that she comes out of her shock.

00:13:46.879 --> 00:13:51.320
Harlan can also repel a bullet fired at him,
just like Vanya did when the Swedes tried

00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:52.740
to shoot her.

00:13:52.740 --> 00:13:57.870
And similar to Vanya in Season 1, when Harlan's
emotions get out of control after the deflected

00:13:57.870 --> 00:14:01.709
bullet accidentally kills his father, he begins
to go supernova.

00:14:01.709 --> 00:14:06.079
Vanya eventually is able to calm him down
when she removes those golden lights from

00:14:06.079 --> 00:14:10.730
his body, however, as we see later when he's
levitating one of his bird toys, he still

00:14:10.730 --> 00:14:13.480
retains at least some of the powers she gave
him.

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:17.089
Which makes me wonder whether Harlan might
grow up to be the father of any of the members

00:14:17.089 --> 00:14:21.749
of the Sparrow Academy or even help form the
group with Hargreeves?

00:14:21.749 --> 00:14:26.500
Season 2 goes deeper into Reginald Hargreeves'
backstory, revealing that he was working for

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:29.709
a time with a shadowy organisation called
the Majestic 12.

00:14:29.709 --> 00:14:34.430
He had a deal to trade them his rocket technology
in return for leaving alone his interests

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:36.439
on the dark side of the moon.

00:14:36.439 --> 00:14:39.649
Hargreeves objected to their assassination
of President Kennedy and attempted to leave

00:14:39.649 --> 00:14:40.670
the group.

00:14:40.670 --> 00:14:44.839
And when they tried to blackmail him, we got
the awesome reveal that he's really an alien

00:14:44.839 --> 00:14:46.779
hiding underneath human skin.

00:14:46.779 --> 00:14:50.900
We only get a glimpse of the back of his head
but the moment is a great nod to the same

00:14:50.900 --> 00:14:54.930
reveal in the comics that Hargreeves wears
a mask to blend in as a human,

00:14:54.930 --> 00:14:57.990
which also explains why he never seems to
age.

00:14:57.990 --> 00:15:01.832
Something I really enjoyed in Season 2 was
getting to learn a lot more about the Commission

00:15:01.832 --> 00:15:06.449
and in particular the Infinite Switchboard
where operators constantly monitor the timeline

00:15:06.449 --> 00:15:07.589
for anomalies.

